  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Diocese of Maralal Drought Relief Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 3 month emergency intervention which will contribute to alleviate the suffering of the hunger stricken communities and livestock as a result of the impact of the current drought in the larger Samburu Districts. This is the second consecutive year of severe drought in the area. The situation has recently worsened even further due to the total failure of the long rains (March-May). 

A recent nutritional survey conducted at national level shows alarming figures. Samburu is amongst the hardest hit districts where rates of global acute malnutrition are currently above 20% which translates in 1 child out of 5 affected by acute malnutrition and highly exposed to high risk of morbidities and motalities. 

The proposed project aims at giving direct support to an estimated 1,500 beneficiaries by providing food aid to vulnerable households and supplementary feeding to 500 children under five who are at risk of acute malnutrition. The project also intends to provide hey and dairy meals to 100 dairy goats thus strengthening the undergoing activities within the Integrated Livelihood and Peace project. This project is also linked to the Disaster Risk Reduction intervention which is being implemented in the areas covered by the Diocese of Maralal.</narrative>
  </description>
